<title>USA: TABLE - Phillips Petroleum Co Q2 profit.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Phillips Petroleum Co Q2 profit.</headline>
<dateline>BARTLESVILLE, Okla. 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.17		    $0.84</p>
<p> Net			307,000		  221,000</p>
<p> Revs		   3,763,000		3,975,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 263,343		  262,949</p>
<p>		     First Half</p>
<p> Shr			  $2.03		    $3.49</p>
<p> Net			534,000		  916,000</p>
<p> Revs		   7,757,000		7,577,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 263,437		  262,629</p>
<p>(All Data Omits 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: Company also reported net operating income of $214 million, or $0.81/shr, for latest quarter saying it excluded special items totaling $93 million.</p>
<p>First Call consensus for quarter was $0.79/shr.</p>
<p>Kenai LNG tax settlement gain of $76 million was main item in 1997 Q2 gains. Also resulted in $571 million gain in 1996 half.</p>
<p>Sweeny, Texas, refining and petrochemical shutdown on power interruption reduced net operating income about $21 million.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
